    "name":  "Cystic fibrosis",
    "module":  "respiratory",
    "category":  "disease",
    "description":  "Cystic fibrosis (CF) is an autosomal recessive disorder caused by mutations in the CFTR gene (most commonly F508del), leading to defective chloride transport and production of thick, viscous secretions in the lungs, pancreas, liver, and reproductive tract. Pulmonary manifestations dominate: chronic productive cough, recurrent lower respiratory tract infections (Pseudomonas aeruginosa, Staphylococcus aureus, Burkholderia cepacia), progressive bronchiectasis, and eventual respiratory failure. Extrapulmonary features include pancreatic exocrine insufficiency (malabsorption, steatorrhoea), CF-related diabetes, and male infertility. Diagnosis is by sweat chloride test and CFTR genotyping. CFTR modulators (elexacaftor/tezacaftor/ivacaftor) have transformed outcomes in eligible patients.",
